/-!
# `Iⁿℱ` is the image of `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ ⟶ ℱ`

Section 08AU of the Stacks project works in Situation 08AV: a Noetherian ring `A` with an ideal
`I`, a proper morphism `f : X ⟶ Spec A` of algebraic spaces and a coherent `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ`.
It denotes by `Iⁿℱ` the quasi-coherent submodule of `ℱ` generated by the products of local
sections of `ℱ` and elements of `Iⁿ`, and says that, in other words, it is the image of the map
`f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ ⟶ ℱ`.  This file proves that second description.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.idealPowerTilde`: the quasi-coherent
  module `Ĩⁿ` on the algebraic space `Spec A`, the associated module on its small étale site of
  the `A`-module `Iⁿ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.idealPowerPullback`: its pullback `f^*Ĩⁿ`
  along the structure morphism, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.idealPowerPullbackι` the map
  `f^*Ĩⁿ ⟶ f^*Ã = 𝒪_X` induced by the inclusion `Iⁿ ⊆ A`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.idealPowerTensorMap`: the map
  `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ ⟶ 𝒪_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ ≅ ℱ`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.imageSubobject_idealPowerTensorMap`:
  **the image of `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ ⟶ ℱ` is `Iⁿℱ`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.idealPowerSubmodule_spec`: the whole of
  Section 08AU, `Iⁿℱ` is quasi-coherent and is the image of `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ ⟶ ℱ`.

## Implementation notes

The tensor product is the tensor product sheaf `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor` of
Stacks 01CA on the small étale ringed site of `X`, the sheafification of the objectwise tensor
product, and `𝒪_X ⊗ ℱ ≅ ℱ` is `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRightUnitIso`.

The argument is categorical.  Write `G` for the functor `M ↦ f^*M̃` from `A`-modules, so that
`f^*Ĩⁿ = G(Iⁿ)` and `G(A) ≅ 𝒪_X`.  It is a composite of left adjoints, so it preserves
colimits, and `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} A ⟶ Iⁿ`, `1_a ↦ a`, is surjective; so the sections
`x_a : 𝒪_X ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ` it induces generate: `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} 𝒪_X ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ` is an epimorphism.  The
composite `𝒪_X ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ ⟶ 𝒪_X` is `G` of multiplication by `a` on `A`, which is multiplication by
the image of `a` in `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.pullbackTildeUnitIso_conj_map_toSpanSingleton`).
Tensoring with `ℱ` preserves colimits (Stacks 05NB) and commutes with multiplication by global
sections, so `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} ℱ ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ` is an epimorphism whose composite with
`f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ ⟶ ℱ` is the map `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} ℱ ⟶ ℱ` whose image is `Iⁿℱ` by definition
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.idealPowerSubmodule`).  An epimorphism does
not change the image.

The image of `a` in `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` is computed in two steps: on `Spec A` the associated module of
multiplication by `a` is multiplication by the global function `a`, read on the identity chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representedAssociatedModuleObjUnitIso_conj_val_app_selfChart`), and
the pullback of multiplication by a global function is multiplication by its image under the
structure map (`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.pullbackModules_map_globalSectionToEnd_unit`),
which on every chart is the pullback of the function along the chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackTerminalSection_hom_app_chartDiagram`).  That is the
definition of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.baseRingHom`.

The statement of Section 08AU writes `f^*Ĩ ⊗ ℱ`; for the submodule `Iⁿℱ` the ideal is `Iⁿ`.

The module universe is the universe of the schemes, as for
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowerSubmodule`:
it is the universe at which the inverse image of modules of Stacks 03LU,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullback`, is defined.  At that universe the abelian structure on
the modules is the one of the small étale ringed site, and the global instances of the
cohomology of modules, stated at a larger universe, are switched off so that instance search
does not try them and leave their universe constraints unsolved.  For the same reason every
coproduct below is indexed by a type with its universe written out.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Section 08AU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08AU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08AV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08AV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05NB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05NB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] isMulCommutative_ringSheaf

namespace FormalFunctionsSituation

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian
  Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesGrothendieck

variable (S : FormalFunctionsSituation.{u, u})

/-- `Spec A` as an algebraic space over itself, the target of the structure morphism of
Situation 08AV: the presheaf represented by the final object of the big fppf site over `Spec A`.
-/
abbrev baseSpace : AlgebraicSpaces S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase :=
  schemeSpace (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)

/-- The structure morphism `f : X ⟶ Spec A` of Situation 08AV, as a morphism of algebraic
spaces. -/
abbrev structureHom : S.space ⟶ baseSpace S :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk S.structureMorphism

/-- The functor `M ↦ M̃` from `A`-modules to modules on the small étale site of the algebraic
space `Spec A`: the associated module of Stacks 03DU (4) of the quasi-coherent module `M̃`. -/
abbrev tildeFunctor : ModuleCat.{u} S.ring ⥤
    Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
      (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2 :=
  tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of S.ring) ⋙
    representedAssociatedModule S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
      (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)
      (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase _)

/-- The functor `M ↦ f^*M̃` from `A`-modules to `𝒪_X`-modules. -/
abbrev pullbackTildeFunctor : ModuleCat.{u} S.ring ⥤
    Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 :=
  tildeFunctor S ⋙ modulePullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)

/-- **The module `Ĩⁿ` on the algebraic space `Spec A`**: the quasi-coherent module associated
with the `A`-module `Iⁿ`. -/
abbrev idealPowerTilde (n : ℕ) :
    Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
      (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2 :=
  (tildeFunctor S).obj (ModuleCat.of S.ring ↥(S.ideal ^ n))

/-- **The pullback `f^*Ĩⁿ`** of `Ĩⁿ` along the structure morphism `f : X ⟶ Spec A`. -/
abbrev idealPowerPullback (n : ℕ) :
    Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 :=
  (modulePullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)).obj
    (idealPowerTilde S n)

/-- The identification `Ã ≅ 𝒪_{Spec A}` on the small étale site of the algebraic space
`Spec A`: the associated module of the structure sheaf is the structure sheaf. -/
def tildeUnitIso :
    (tildeFunctor S).obj (ModuleCat.of S.ring S.ring) ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
          (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O) :=
  representedAssociatedModuleObjUnitIso S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
    (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)
    (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase _)

/-- The identification `f^*Ã ≅ 𝒪_X`: the associated module of `Ã = 𝒪_{Spec A}` is the structure
sheaf of the algebraic space `Spec A`, and the pullback of the structure sheaf is the structure
sheaf. -/
def pullbackTildeUnitIso :
    (pullbackTildeFunctor S).obj (ModuleCat.of S.ring S.ring) ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O) :=
  (modulePullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)).mapIso
      (tildeUnitIso S) ≪≫
    modulePullbackUnitIso S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)

/-- **The map `f^*Ĩⁿ ⟶ 𝒪_X`**: the pullback of the map `Ĩⁿ ⟶ Ã = 𝒪_{Spec A}` induced by the
inclusion `Iⁿ ⊆ A`, followed by `f^*𝒪_{Spec A} ≅ 𝒪_X`. -/
def idealPowerPullbackι (n : ℕ) :
    idealPowerPullback S n ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O) :=
  (pullbackTildeFunctor S).map (ModuleCat.ofHom (S.ideal ^ n).subtype) ≫
    (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).hom

/-- The tensor product functor `- ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ` on `𝒪_X`-modules: the tensor product sheaf of
Stacks 01CA on the small étale ringed site of `X`. -/
abbrev tensorCoefficients :
    Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 ⥤
      Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 :=
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u + 1, u, u, u, u}
    (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O).flip.obj
      S.coefficients

/-- **The map `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ ⟶ ℱ`** of Section 08AU: `f^*Ĩⁿ ⟶ 𝒪_X` tensored with `ℱ`,
followed by `𝒪_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ ≅ ℱ`. -/
def idealPowerTensorMap (n : ℕ) :
    (tensorCoefficients S).obj (idealPowerPullback S n) ⟶ S.coefficients :=
  (tensorCoefficients S).map (idealPowerPullbackι S n) ≫
    (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRightUnitIso
      (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O
      S.coefficients).hom

/-! ### Multiplication by an element of `A`, pulled back to `X` -/

/-- The commutative diagram of étale scheme charts over the structure morphism `f : X ⟶ Spec A`
attached to an étale scheme chart `W` of `X`: the target chart is the identity chart of
`Spec A`, and the vertical morphism is the structure morphism of `W`. -/
def baseChartDiagram (W : SmallEtale S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1) :
    ChartDiagram S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 (baseSpace S).1
      (structureHom S).hom where
  U := W
  V := selfChart S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)
  g := (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := S.site.obj S.containsBase)).from _
  comm := ((Over.mkIdTerminal (X := S.site.obj S.containsBase)).isTerminalObj yoneda _).hom_ext _ _

/-- On the identity chart of `Spec A`, the endomorphism of `𝒪_{Spec A}` induced by
multiplication by `a ∈ A` takes `1` to the global function `a`. -/
theorem tildeUnitIso_conj_map_toSpanSingleton_val_app_selfChart (a : S.ring) :
    ((tildeUnitIso S).inv ≫
        (tildeFunctor S).map (ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S.ring S.ring a)) ≫
          (tildeUnitIso S).hom).val.app
        (op (selfChart S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
          (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)))
        (1 : Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase).obj
          (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase), ⊤)) =
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of S.ring)).inv a :=
  (representedAssociatedModuleObjUnitIso_conj_val_app_selfChart S.site (Spec (.of S.ring))
    S.containsBase (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)
    ((tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of S.ring)).map
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S.ring S.ring a)))).trans
    (tilde_map_toSpanSingleton_val_app_top_one (CommRingCat.of S.ring) a)

/-- **The image under `f♯` of the global function of `Spec A` given by `a ∈ A` is the image of
`a` in `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`**: on every chart of `X` it is the pullback of `a` along the chart.  The
global function is given as the section `t(1)` of an endomorphism `t` of `𝒪_{Spec A}`, read
through `Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.unitEndSection`. -/
theorem terminalHomEquivSections_pullbackTerminalSection_eq_baseRingHom (a : S.ring)
    (t : SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
          (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
          (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O))
    (ht : t.val.app (op (selfChart S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
        (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)))
        (1 : Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase).obj
          (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase), ⊤)) =
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of S.ring)).inv a) :
    Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O))
        (Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.pullbackTerminalSection
          (X := smallEtaleRingedTopos S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space)
          (Y := smallEtaleRingedTopos S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S))
          (smallEtaleRingedToposModulesHom S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
            (structureHom S))
          ((Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O))).symm
            ⟨(unitEndSection _ t).1, (unitEndSection _ t).2⟩)) =
      ⟨(baseRingHom S.ring S.site S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 a).1,
        (baseRingHom S.ring S.site S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 a).2⟩ := by
  refine Subtype.ext (funext fun W => ?_)
  refine (pullbackTerminalSection_hom_app_chartDiagram S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
    (structureHom S) (baseChartDiagram S W.unop)
    ((Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O))).symm
            ⟨(unitEndSection _ t).1, (unitEndSection _ t).2⟩)).trans ?_
  refine (congrArg (chartDiagramPullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
    (structureHom S) (baseChartDiagram S W.unop)).hom ht).trans ?_
  have e : (baseChartDiagram S W.unop).g.left =
      ((SmallEtale.toOver S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1).obj W.unop).hom :=
    Over.mkIdTerminal_from_left _
  show Scheme.Γ.map (S.site.inclusion.map (baseChartDiagram S W.unop).g.left).op
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of S.ring)).inv a) = _
  rw [e]
  rfl

/-- The pullback along `f` of an endomorphism `t` of `𝒪_{Spec A}`, read on `𝒪_X` through
`f^*𝒪_{Spec A} ≅ 𝒪_X`, is multiplication by the image under `f♯` of the global function
`t(1)`. -/
theorem modulePullbackUnitIso_conj_map (t : SheafOfModules.unit
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring))
        S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
          (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O)) :
    (modulePullbackUnitIso S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)).inv ≫
        (modulePullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)).map t ≫
          (modulePullbackUnitIso S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)).hom =
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring))
          S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O)
        (Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O))
        (Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.pullbackTerminalSection
          (X := smallEtaleRingedTopos S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space)
          (Y := smallEtaleRingedTopos S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S))
          (smallEtaleRingedToposModulesHom S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
            (structureHom S))
          ((Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O))).symm
            ⟨(unitEndSection _ t).1, (unitEndSection _ t).2⟩)))).app (SheafOfModules.unit _) := by
  have h2 : t = (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring))
          S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O)
      (Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O))
          ((Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O))).symm
        ⟨(unitEndSection _ t).1, (unitEndSection _ t).2⟩))).app (SheafOfModules.unit _) :=
    (eq_globalSmul_unitEndSection _ t).trans
      (congrArg (fun x => (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd _ x).app
        (SheafOfModules.unit _)) (Equiv.apply_symm_apply _ _).symm)
  have h3 := Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.pullbackModules_map_globalSectionToEnd_unit
    (X := smallEtaleRingedTopos S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space)
    (Y := smallEtaleRingedTopos S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S))
    (smallEtaleRingedToposModulesHom S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S))
    ((Sheaf.terminalHomEquivSections (Sheaf.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site
            (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (baseSpace S).1 (baseSpace S).2).O))).symm
            ⟨(unitEndSection _ t).1, (unitEndSection _ t).2⟩)
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc
    (Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.pullbackModulesObjUnitIso
      (smallEtaleRingedToposModulesHom S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
        (structureHom S))) _)
  refine congrArg (fun m => (Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.pullbackModulesObjUnitIso
      (smallEtaleRingedToposModulesHom S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
        (structureHom S))).hom ≫ m) (Eq.trans ?_ h3)
  exact congrArg (fun m => (modulePullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
    (structureHom S)).map m ≫ _) h2

/-- **`G` carries multiplication by `a ∈ A` on `A` to multiplication by the image of `a` in
`Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`**, for the functor `G : M ↦ f^*M̃` and the identification `G(A) ≅ 𝒪_X`. -/
theorem pullbackTildeUnitIso_conj_map_toSpanSingleton (a : S.ring) :
    (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).inv ≫
        (pullbackTildeFunctor S).map (ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S.ring S.ring a)) ≫
          (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).hom =
      globalSmul _ (baseRingHom S.ring S.site S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 a) _ := by
  have h1 : (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).inv ≫
      (pullbackTildeFunctor S).map (ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S.ring S.ring a)) ≫
        (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).hom =
      (modulePullbackUnitIso S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)).inv ≫
        (modulePullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)).map
          ((tildeUnitIso S).inv ≫
            (tildeFunctor S).map (ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S.ring S.ring a)) ≫
              (tildeUnitIso S).hom) ≫
          (modulePullbackUnitIso S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
            (structureHom S)).hom := by
    simp only [pullbackTildeUnitIso, Iso.trans_inv, Iso.trans_hom, Functor.mapIso_inv,
      Functor.mapIso_hom, Functor.comp_map, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc]
  refine h1.trans ((modulePullbackUnitIso_conj_map S _).trans ?_)
  exact congrArg (fun x => (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd _ x).app
    (SheafOfModules.unit _))
    (terminalHomEquivSections_pullbackTerminalSection_eq_baseRingHom S a _
      (tildeUnitIso_conj_map_toSpanSingleton_val_app_selfChart S a))

/-! ### The sections `x_a` of `f^*Ĩⁿ` generate it -/

/-- `M ↦ f^*M̃` commutes with colimits: it is a composite of left adjoints, the passage
`M ↦ M̃` to quasi-coherent modules on `Spec A`, the associated module on its small étale site,
and the pullback along `f`. -/
instance preservesColimitsOfSize_pullbackTildeFunctor :
    PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (pullbackTildeFunctor S) := by
  have h1 : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (representedModulePushforward S.site (Spec (.of S.ring))
      S.containsBase (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)) :=
    (representedSmallEtaleModuleEquivalence S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
      (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)).toAdjunction.leftAdjoint_preservesColimits
  have h2 : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u}
      (representedAssociatedModule S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
        (baseObject S.ring S.site S.containsBase)
        (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase _)) :=
    @comp_preservesColimits _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ inferInstance h1
  have h0 : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of S.ring)) :=
    tilde.adjunction.leftAdjoint_preservesColimits
  have h3 : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u}
      (modulePullback S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase (structureHom S)) :=
    (modulePullbackAdjunction S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase
      (structureHom S)).leftAdjoint_preservesColimits
  have h4 : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (tildeFunctor S) :=
    @comp_preservesColimits _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ h0 h2
  exact @comp_preservesColimits _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ h4 h3

/-- The map `A ⟶ Iⁿ`, `1 ↦ a`, for `a ∈ Iⁿ`. -/
abbrev idealPowerElement (n : ℕ) (a : ↥(S.ideal ^ n)) :
    ModuleCat.of S.ring S.ring ⟶ ModuleCat.of S.ring ↥(S.ideal ^ n) :=
  ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S.ring ↥(S.ideal ^ n) a)

/-- The surjection `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} A ⟶ Iⁿ`, `1_a ↦ a`. -/
theorem epi_sigmaDesc_idealPowerElement (n : ℕ) :
    Epi (Sigma.desc (idealPowerElement S n)) := by
  refine (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective _).2 fun b => ⟨(Sigma.ι (fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) =>
    ModuleCat.of S.ring S.ring) b).hom 1, ?_⟩
  refine (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (Sigma.ι_desc (idealPowerElement S n) b) 1).trans ?_
  exact one_smul S.ring b

/-- A functor preserving the coproduct of `f` and the pushout of an epimorphism `g` out of it
carries `g`, precomposed with the coproduct comparison, to an epimorphism. -/
private theorem epi_sigmaComparison_comp_map {C D : Type*} [Category C] [Category D]
    (F : C ⥤ D) {ι : Type*} (f : ι → C) [HasCoproduct f] [HasCoproduct fun i => F.obj (f i)]
    [PreservesColimit (Discrete.functor f) F] {Y : C} (g : ∐ f ⟶ Y) [Epi g]
    [PreservesColimit (span g g) F] : Epi (sigmaComparison F f ≫ F.map g) := by
  have : IsIso (sigmaComparison F f) := by
    rw [← PreservesCoproduct.inv_hom]
    exact Iso.isIso_inv _
  have : Epi (F.map g) := preserves_epi_of_preservesColimit _ _
  exact epi_comp _ _

/-- **The section `x_a` of `f^*Ĩⁿ`** attached to `a ∈ Iⁿ`: `f^*` of the map `𝒪_{Spec A} ⟶ Ĩⁿ`,
`1 ↦ a`, read on `𝒪_X`. -/
def idealPowerSection (n : ℕ) (a : ↥(S.ideal ^ n)) :
    SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O) ⟶
      idealPowerPullback S n :=
  (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).inv ≫ (pullbackTildeFunctor S).map (idealPowerElement S n a)

/-- The map `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} 𝒪_X ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ` whose component at `a` is the section `x_a`. -/
abbrev idealPowerSectionSum (n : ℕ) :
    (∐ fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) => (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O) :
        Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2)) ⟶
      idealPowerPullback S n :=
  Sigma.desc (idealPowerSection S n)

/-- **The sections `x_a`, `a ∈ Iⁿ`, generate `f^*Ĩⁿ`**: `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} 𝒪_X ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ` is an
epimorphism. -/
theorem epi_idealPowerSectionSum (n : ℕ) : Epi (idealPowerSectionSum S n) := by
  have e : idealPowerSectionSum S n =
      Limits.Sigma.map (fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) => (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).inv) ≫
        sigmaComparison (pullbackTildeFunctor S) (fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) =>
          ModuleCat.of S.ring S.ring) ≫
          (pullbackTildeFunctor S).map (Sigma.desc (idealPowerElement S n)) := by
    refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun a => ?_
    rw [Sigma.ι_desc, sigmaComparison_map_desc, Limits.Sigma.ι_map_assoc, Sigma.ι_desc]
    rfl
  have := epi_sigmaDesc_idealPowerElement S n
  have : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{0, 0} (pullbackTildeFunctor S) :=
    preservesSmallestColimits_of_preservesColimits _
  have := epi_sigmaComparison_comp_map (pullbackTildeFunctor S)
    (fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) => ModuleCat.of S.ring S.ring) (Sigma.desc (idealPowerElement S n))
  have : Epi (Limits.Sigma.map (fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) => (pullbackTildeUnitIso S).inv)) :=
    Limits.Sigma.map_epi _
  rw [e]
  exact epi_comp _ _

/-- The section `x_a` followed by `f^*Ĩⁿ ⟶ 𝒪_X` is multiplication by the image of `a` in
`Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`. -/
theorem idealPowerSection_comp_idealPowerPullbackι (n : ℕ) (a : ↥(S.ideal ^ n)) :
    idealPowerSection S n a ≫ idealPowerPullbackι S n =
      globalSmul _ (baseRingHom S.ring S.site S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2 a.1) _ := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (pullbackTildeUnitIso_conj_map_toSpanSingleton S a.1)
  have e : idealPowerElement S n a ≫ ModuleCat.ofHom (S.ideal ^ n).subtype =
      ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S.ring S.ring a.1) :=
    ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun _ => rfl)
  simp only [idealPowerSection, idealPowerPullbackι, Category.assoc, ← Functor.map_comp_assoc, e]

/-! ### The image of `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ ⟶ ℱ` -/

/-- Tensoring with `ℱ` commutes with colimits (Stacks 05NB). -/
instance preservesColimitsOfSize_tensorCoefficients :
    PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (tensorCoefficients S) := by
  have h : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u} (tensorCoefficients S) :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.FlatSheafification.sheafTensorRight_preservesColimits
      (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).J
      (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O
      S.coefficients
  exact preservesColimitsOfSize_shrink.{u, u, u, u + 1} _

/-- The map `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} 𝒪_X ⊗ ℱ ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ` induced by the sections `x_a`. -/
abbrev idealPowerTensorSum (n : ℕ) :
    (∐ fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) => (tensorCoefficients S).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O))) ⟶
      (tensorCoefficients S).obj (idealPowerPullback S n) :=
  Sigma.desc fun a => (tensorCoefficients S).map (idealPowerSection S n a)

/-- The map `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} 𝒪_X ⊗ ℱ ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ` induced by the sections `x_a` is an
epimorphism. -/
theorem epi_idealPowerTensorSum (n : ℕ) : Epi (idealPowerTensorSum S n) := by
  have hT : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (tensorCoefficients S) :=
    preservesColimitsOfSize_tensorCoefficients S
  have hT0 : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{0, 0} (tensorCoefficients S) :=
    @preservesSmallestColimits_of_preservesColimits _ _ _ _ _ hT
  have p1 : PreservesColimit (Discrete.functor fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) =>
      (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O) :
        Modules.{u, u} S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2))
      (tensorCoefficients S) :=
    hT.preservesColimitsOfShape.preservesColimit
  have p2 : PreservesColimit (span (idealPowerSectionSum S n) (idealPowerSectionSum S n))
      (tensorCoefficients S) :=
    hT0.preservesColimitsOfShape.preservesColimit
  have := epi_idealPowerSectionSum S n
  rw [idealPowerTensorSum, ← sigmaComparison_map_desc]
  exact epi_sigmaComparison_comp_map (tensorCoefficients S) _ (idealPowerSectionSum S n)

/-- The composite `⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} 𝒪_X ⊗ ℱ ⟶ f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ ⟶ ℱ` is, through `𝒪_X ⊗ ℱ ≅ ℱ`, the map
`⨁_{a ∈ Iⁿ} ℱ ⟶ ℱ` whose component at `a` is multiplication by `a`. -/
theorem idealPowerTensorSum_comp_idealPowerTensorMap (n : ℕ) :
    idealPowerTensorSum S n ≫ idealPowerTensorMap S n =
      Limits.Sigma.map (fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) =>
        (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRightUnitIso
        (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O
        S.coefficients).hom) ≫ idealPowerSmulHom S n := by
  refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun a => ?_
  rw [idealPowerTensorSum, Sigma.ι_desc_assoc, Limits.Sigma.ι_map_assoc, Sigma.ι_desc,
    idealPowerTensorMap,
    ← Functor.map_comp_assoc, idealPowerSection_comp_idealPowerPullbackι]
  refine (congrArg (fun m => m ≫ (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRightUnitIso
    (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O
    S.coefficients).hom)
    (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRight_map_globalSectionToEnd
      (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O
      S.coefficients _ _)).trans ?_
  exact (comp_globalSmul _ _ _).symm

/-- **`Iⁿℱ` is the image of `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ ⟶ ℱ`** (Section 08AU), in Situation 08AV: as
subobjects of `ℱ`, the image of the map `f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ ⟶ 𝒪_X ⊗ ℱ ≅ ℱ` is the submodule `Iⁿℱ`
generated by the products of local sections of `ℱ` and elements of `Iⁿ`. -/
@[stacks 08AU "Iⁿℱ is the image of f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ → ℱ, in Situation 08AV; the source writes f^*Ĩ \
for the ideal Iⁿ of the submodule Iⁿℱ"]
theorem imageSubobject_idealPowerTensorMap (n : ℕ) :
    imageSubobject (idealPowerTensorMap S n) = Subobject.mk (idealPowerSubmoduleι S n) := by
  have hE := epi_idealPowerTensorSum S n
  have hle := imageSubobject_comp_le (idealPowerTensorSum S n) (idealPowerTensorMap S n)
  have : IsIso (Subobject.ofLE _ _ hle) := isIso_of_mono_of_epi _
  have h2 : imageSubobject (idealPowerTensorSum S n ≫ idealPowerTensorMap S n) =
      imageSubobject (idealPowerTensorMap S n) :=
    le_antisymm hle (Subobject.le_of_comm (inv (Subobject.ofLE _ _ hle))
      ((IsIso.inv_comp_eq _).2 (Subobject.ofLE_arrow hle).symm))
  have h3 : imageSubobject (idealPowerTensorSum S n ≫ idealPowerTensorMap S n) =
      imageSubobject (Limits.Sigma.map (fun _ : ↥(S.ideal ^ n) =>
        (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRightUnitIso
          (smallEtaleRingedSite S.site (Spec (.of S.ring)) S.containsBase S.space.1 S.space.2).O
          S.coefficients).hom) ≫ idealPowerSmulHom S n) := by
    rw [idealPowerTensorSum_comp_idealPowerTensorMap]
  exact h2.symm.trans (h3.trans (imageSubobject_iso_comp _ _))

/-- **Section 08AU**, in Situation 08AV: the submodule `Iⁿℱ` of `ℱ` generated by the products of
local sections of `ℱ` and elements of `Iⁿ` is quasi-coherent, and it is the image of the map
`f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℱ ⟶ ℱ`. -/
@[stacks 08AU "Iⁿℱ is a quasi-coherent submodule of ℱ and is the image of f^*Ĩⁿ ⊗ ℱ → ℱ, in \
Situation 08AV"]
theorem idealPowerSubmodule_spec (n : ℕ) :
    (idealPowerSubmodule S n).IsQuasicoherentOnSite ∧
      imageSubobject (idealPowerTensorMap S n) = Subobject.mk (idealPowerSubmoduleι S n) :=
  ⟨isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowerSubmodule S n, imageSubobject_idealPowerTensorMap S n⟩

